                  "content": "A comprehensive logging and monitoring strategy will be implemented:\n\n*   **Logging:** Use Laravel's built-in logging system to log application events, errors, and warnings. Configure a dedicated `stderr` channel for production to log directly to the system's standard error stream.\n*   **Structured Logging:** Use structured logging (e.g., JSON) to make logs easier to parse and analyze.\n*   **Centralized Logging:** Aggregate logs from all application instances into a central logging system (e.g., Elasticsearch, Graylog, Splunk). Utilize Laravel's monolog integration [https://github.com/Seldaek/monolog].\n*   **Monitoring:** Monitor key metrics (e.g., CPU usage, memory usage, response time, error rate) using a monitoring tool (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana, New Relic).\n*   **Alerting:** Set up alerts to notify administrators when critical metrics exceed predefined thresholds.  Implement health checks for all services.\n*   **Tracing:** Implement distributed tracing (e.g., Jaeger, Zipkin) to track requests across multiple services and identify performance bottlenecks.\n*   **Exception Tracking:** Use an exception tracking service (e.g., Sentry) to capture and analyze application exceptions.\n\nThis will allow for proactive identification and resolution of issues.",
